error Failure { Failed; }

// The logical connectives `||` and `&&` in an `if` condition (card
// `OR-AND-LOWERING`), lowered onto `source.branch.v1` (card `IF-STATEMENT`).
//
// A connective is a **pure token-tier construct**: it adds no operation, no
// checker rule and no core IR node. `A || B` is the right-nested branch a
// reader would have written by hand as `if (A) { … } else if (B) { … } else
// { … }`, and this fixture's emitted C is byte-identical to that twin's.
//
// Short-circuit is structural rather than asserted: `2 == 2` is the condition
// of a branch that sits inside the *else* arm of `3 < 5`'s branch, so the
// emitted C reaches it on exactly one path.
//
// The custody join is unmoved. Each connective level runs the same four-model
// join, so the arms of this branch must still agree — which is why both of
// them release, and why releasing on only one is still the conditional leak.
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = qcore_acquire(1, true, Failure);
    if (3 < 5 || 2 == 2) {
        drop a;
    } else {
        drop a;
    }
    return 0;
}
